{"audit": {"coverageKind": "diagnoses", "state": "unaudited"}, "id": "2006_sprinkle_collins.d:0/children/0/children/0/children/0:diagnosis", "kind": "diagnosis", "path": "0/children/0/children/0/children/0", "printedAttribution": "as-record", "source": "2006_sprinkle_collins.d", "subject": "lyracystidae", "text": "Eocrinoids having numerous, irregular, ridged thecal plates\nbearing epispires; three large distinctive lyre-shaped arms with\nnumerous long, straight brachioles attached in central V; and\na long multiplated stalk for attachment with domed, ridged,\nor spiny small plates.\n", "tree": "taxonomy"}
