{"actKind": "new", "audit": {"coverageKind": "newTaxa", "state": "unaudited"}, "id": "2006_sprinkle_collins.d:0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/1:act", "kind": "act", "path": "0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/1", "printedAttribution": "as-record", "source": "2006_sprinkle_collins.d", "subject": "reesei_sprinkle_collins.d_2006", "tree": "taxonomy"}
{"audit": {"coverageKind": "diagnoses", "state": "unaudited"}, "id": "2006_sprinkle_collins.d:0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/1:diagnosis", "kind": "diagnosis", "path": "0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/1", "printedAttribution": "as-record", "source": "2006_sprinkle_collins.d", "subject": "reesei_sprinkle_collins.d_2006", "text": "Theca rounded conical, slightly longer than wide with domed\nsummit, having about 60 primary and smaller secondary plates\nwith scattered epispires on best side, 5–7 vertical ridges\nextending up from four basals, intersecting low horizontal\nridge in mid-theca; only proximal segments of two lyre-shaped?\nbiserial arms with smaller brachioles preserved; multiplated\nstalk very long, thin, slowly tapering away from thecal\nattachment, ridged proximally and spiny medially, distal\nattachment holdfast inferred but not preserved.\n", "tree": "taxonomy"}
