{"audit": {"coverageKind": "diagnoses", "state": "unaudited"}, "id": "2006_sprinkle_collins.d:0/children/0/children/0/children/1/children/0/children/1:diagnosis", "kind": "diagnosis", "path": "0/children/0/children/0/children/1/children/0/children/1", "printedAttribution": "as-record", "source": "2006_sprinkle_collins.d", "subject": "stephenensis_sprinkle_collins.d_2006", "text": "Gogia with an ellipsoidal to rounded conical theca with\nmoderate number of large and small plates, many elliptical\nepispires on larger thecal plates all over theca, relatively\nshort thin stalk with many small plates, often flared distally\ninto an enlarged circular structure, and 10–12 long, mostly\nstraight brachioles that rarely spiral and may branch.\n", "tree": "taxonomy"}
